<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yoga</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yoga is a group of physical, mental and spiritual practices that originated in ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, aimed at controlling body and mind to attain liberation (moksha), as practised in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a>, Jain and Buddhist traditions. It may have pre-Vedic origins but is first attested in the early first millennium BCE, and systematic yoga concepts emerged in the fifth and sixth centuries BCE in the ascetic and Śramaṇa movements. The Yoga Sutras of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patanjali">Patanjali</a>, the classical text on Hindu yoga, date to the early centuries of the Common Era, and hatha yoga texts appeared between the ninth and 11th centuries. Modern forms, largely made up of asanas, spread worldwide after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swami-vivekananda">Swami Vivekananda</a>'s adaptation.</p></div>
